<section style="padding:4rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div style="max-width:800px;">
      <p style="font-size:0.6rem;letter-spacing:0.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#e00;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Inside the Factory</p>
      <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Production Line Structure &amp; Quality Checkpoints</h2>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.9;margin-bottom:1rem;">A bulk order moves through distinct in-house departments: fabric inspection and relaxation, computerized cutting (marker-making optimized to minimize fabric waste), sewing lines organized by operation (each operator handles one construction step, not the whole garment), finishing (trimming, pressing, folding), and final packing. Keeping every stage under one roof in Baridhara DOHS removes the handoff delays and quality gaps that come with sub-contracting any single step to an outside unit.</p>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.9;">Quality control happens at three checkpoints, not just at the end: incoming fabric inspection (4-point system, checking for defects before cutting even starts), in-line inspection during sewing (catching construction errors early, before a defect is repeated across hundreds of pieces), and final AQL 2.5 inspection before packing. Catching a problem at the in-line stage, rather than after the whole run is sewn, is what actually keeps rework and late shipments rare.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="padding:4rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <p style="font-size:0.6rem;letter-spacing:0.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#e00;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Common Questions</p>
    <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Garments Factory FAQ</h2>
    <div style="max-width:800px;">
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Can I visit the factory in person before placing an order?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Yes, B2B factory visits are welcome with advance notice — see our factory visit booking page for scheduling. Virtual factory tours over video call are also available for buyers who can't travel to Bangladesh.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Do you subcontract any part of production to outside factories?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">No — cutting, sewing, finishing, and packing all happen at our own Baridhara DOHS facility. This is a deliberate choice: sub-contracted stages are a common source of quality inconsistency and delayed communication that we avoid by keeping everything in-house.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What happens if a quality issue is found during in-line inspection?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">The affected operation is stopped and corrected before more pieces move through that step, and any already-affected pieces are pulled for rework or replacement — catching the issue at this stage prevents it from reaching final inspection at volume.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Can third-party auditors inspect the factory for compliance?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Yes. As a BSCI socially compliant, WRAP accredited facility, we regularly undergo third-party social and quality audits and can accommodate buyer-nominated auditors as part of a new order agreement.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

